# ---- HOST-NATIVE STATION (de-bridged 2026-08-16, VICE wave #1) ----
# VICE 3.10.0's xvic runs ON THE HOST, headless: no QEMU, no guest Debian, no
# X server, no kiosk. Frames: the fork's shm publisher (VICE_SHM_PATH) ->
# SH_CAPTURE=shm, the same IFB1 wire format MAME's drawshm uses. Keys: the
# vicectl unix socket + the ONE shared generated keysym table (VICE resolves
# keysym -> matrix through the machine's own gtk3_sym.vkm, which is why this
# station needs no charMap and no per-station matrix map). Audio: -sounddev
# wav -> named FIFO, the daemon is the clock. Launcher: the shared
# stations/vice-native/x11-runtime.sh; VICE_NATIVE_* are its knobs.
# Build: scripts/build-guests/emulators/build-vice-native.sh vic20.
SH_RESET_MODE=relaunch
SH_FIXTURE_DESC=Commodore VIC-20 (PAL) ROM BASIC power-on screen — "**** CBM BASIC V2 **** / 3583 BYTES FREE / READY." in blue on white paper inside a cyan border, drawn double-size (-VICdsize) with full borders (-VICborders 0) by host-native VICE 3.10.0 xvic. PUBLISHED SURFACE 896x568, MEASURED off the shm mapping (2 035 776 B = 64 + 896*568*4) — VICE has no MAME_SHM_SIZE equivalent, the surface IS the emulated screen times VICDoubleSize, so this geometry follows from VICE_NATIVE_ARGS and nothing else. Nothing is curated and nothing is typed; the checkpoint in sta/golden.vsf is an untouched cold boot. Keyboard-only exhibit; no pointer device; VIC-I sound -> FIFO.
VICE_NATIVE_BIN=/data/vms/streamhost/assets/vic20/vice-native/bin/xvic
VICE_NATIVE_DATA=/data/vms/streamhost/assets/vic20/vice-native/share/vice
# The ONLY thing that decides the published geometry (see SH_FIXTURE_DESC).
VICE_NATIVE_ARGS=-pal -VICdsize -VICborders 0
SH_VICECTL_SOCK=/data/vms/streamhost/stations/vic20/ctl.sock
SH_VICESOCK_KEYMAP=/data/vms/streamhost/stations/vic20/us-layout.keysyms
SH_AUDIO_SOURCE=fifo
SH_AUDIO_FIFO=/data/vms/streamhost/stations/vic20/audio.fifo

# ---- STANDBY (instant-ready: an emulator nobody watches costs ~0 CPU) ----
# The launcher freezes the emulator once the scene has painted and the daemon
# owns it from there: SIGSTOP after the idle grace with zero sessions, an
# unconditional SIGCONT the moment a visitor connects. WITHOUT THESE TWO LINES
# A DE-BRIDGED STATION BURNS A FULL CORE AROUND THE CLOCK.
# SH_IDLE_PAUSE_PROC_MATCH is the anti-footgun: the signal only ever reaches a
# pid whose cmdline still carries THIS station's own asset path — six more VICE
# stations are coming and several will share a binary name (xpet serves both
# pet2001 and cbm8032).
# Rollback is one line: SH_IDLE_PAUSE_SECS=0 restores an always-running exhibit.
SH_IDLE_PAUSE_SECS=60
SH_IDLE_PAUSE_PIDFILE=/data/vms/streamhost/stations/vic20/vice.pid
SH_IDLE_PAUSE_PROC_MATCH=assets/vic20/vice-native
VICE_NATIVE_STANDBY_DELAY_S=8

# ---- KEYBOARD PACING (the exhibit's only input surface) ----
# RE-BISECTED against THIS engine on 2026-08-16, not inherited: the bridged
# 80/80 was measured against QEMU send-key into an SDL kiosk, a completely
# different path. Method: the bridged bisect's own (restore the same
# checkpoint, type one fixed 40-character line, compare the FRAMEBUFFER — here
# the shm mapping itself — against a 250/250 reference with the blinking
# cursor masked out), run on a clone under /data/vms/soltest/vice-vic20.
#
#   hold/gap   corrupted lines of 12    max unmasked delta
#   20/20      0                        0
#   40/40      0                        0
#   60/60      0                        0
#   80/80      0                        0
#
# Nothing corrupts, at any pacing tested, because on this path pacing lives
# INSIDE the emulator: vicectl drains its queue per key at emulated-frame
# boundaries and VICE_CTL_KEY_EXCL=1 serializes the matrix, so the browser's
# one-burst delivery can no longer collapse two presses into one frame. The
# bridged failure mode (a host stall swallowing both edges of a keystroke
# between two input pumps) cannot happen when the dwell is counted in the
# guest's own frames.
# 60/60 SHIPS ANYWAY — the module's own default, one clean step below the
# bridged 80/80: it types visibly faster than the kiosk did while keeping two
# clear frames of margin over the last pacing that was ever observed to fail
# anywhere in the lab. The launcher hands these two to the module as
# VICE_CTL_KEY_HOLD/_GAP.
SH_KEY_MIN_HOLD_MS=60
SH_KEY_MIN_GAP_MS=60
# demoProgram.perCharMs (170) stays >= HOLD+GAP: the SPA typist waits
# line.length * perCharMs before submitting the next line, and under-waiting
# builds a backlog whose symptom is missing characters.
# No SH_KEY_MAP: this machine's matrix does not have to be re-derived, and
# unlike the MAME stations there is no per-station keymap file at all. VICE's
# own symbolic keymap (VIC20/gtk3_sym.vkm, staged by the builder) maps the
# host keysym to the Commodore key that produces that character. What the SPA
# must know is that the machine is upper-case-only — a SHIFTED letter on a
# VIC-20 is a graphics glyph — which registry `keyboard.letterCase` declares
# and the SPA typist honours by sending letters unshifted.
